From 7454309f739abe94d82f9d29f0b396ba1bdd6c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris <christopher@deocracy.org>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 16:21:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] property: don't wait out the timeout on writes denied by the
 whitelist (D678)

On DIGIC 678X ports, prop_request_change() silently drops any write to
a property that is not in the port's prop_write_allow[] whitelist.
prop_request_change_wait() still polls for the ack afterwards - an ack
that can never arrive, because no write was issued - so every denied
write burns the full timeout.

The practical impact: PROP_ICU_UILOCK is whitelisted on no DIGIC 7
body, so every gui_uilock() call is a 2000 ms stall. mlv_lite wraps
each buffer reallocation in a gui_uilock() pair from its polling loop,
which turns raw-video startup into a chain of 2 s freezes. Diagnosed
on a 6D2 from on-camera console output: repeated 'UILock: ... =>
00000000 (!!!)' (gui-common.c's mismatch marker) immediately before a
freeze at SRM allocation.

Bail out before issuing the write instead: if the property is not
whitelisted the change is known not to happen, and waiting for its ack
is pure delay. Returning 0 keeps the existing 'not confirmed' contract
for callers. No new writes are issued anywhere; the change only waits
less.

Tested: builds clean for 6D2.111; deployed to a real 6D2, on-camera
retest of the raw-video path still pending.
---
 src/property.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/property.c b/src/property.c
index f824dfa25..2a96edd25 100755
--- a/src/property.c
+++ b/src/property.c
@@ -409,6 +409,14 @@ ok:
 
 int prop_request_change_wait(unsigned property, const void* addr, size_t len, int timeout)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_DIGIC_678X
+    /* On D678, prop_request_change() silently drops writes to properties not
+     * in prop_write_allow[].  Waiting for an ack from a write that was never
+     * issued just burns the full timeout (2s per gui_uilock() call, from
+     * mlv_lite's polling loop among others).  Bail out up front instead. */
+    if (!is_prop_allowed(property))
+        return 0;
+#endif
     prop_reset_ack(property);
     prop_request_change(property, addr, len);
     
-- 
2.54.0

